I go to a small kirana shop on the corner.
An elderly man is behind the counter.
I say hello to him.
He smiles and says, "Hello madam."
He asks, "What do you want?"
I look at my list.
I want some essential spices.
I say, "Chacha, I want turmeric and cumin."
"And I also want one packet of salt."
Chacha gives me those spices.
He asks, "Do you want anything else?"
I like India's spicy food very much.
I say, "Yes, I also want some red chili."
Chacha takes out a small packet.
He gives me all the items.
I give the money to Chacha.
Now I have all the essential spices.
I come out of the shop.
